Hi Marcus,

During the automated profiling of the DAQ dataset, our ingestion quality gate identified and isolated 17 non-canonical CSV files into quarantine:
- 12 files quarantined for column_count_mismatch (missing Z_Load_Cell or Current columns from legacy 4-channel DAQ card tests).
- 4 files quarantined for null_bytes / non_numeric_signal_values due to incomplete buffer flush during emergency machine stop.
- 1 file quarantined for missing_header.

Total discovered files: 822.
Total canonical files approved for baseline analytics: 805.

Per the strict quality policy in config/domain.yaml, quarantined files will remain segregated in quarantine.jsonl and will NOT be coerced, repaired, or fed into Mahalanobis baseline computation.

Rachel Torres
